  "section_notes": "The final standard is mostly safety-forward: S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all incidents and 48-hour customer notice; S2 sets a 55 °C/5% test with regulator confidentiality and customer/prospective-buyer access but no automatic sales stop; S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit with alternative isolation; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 incidents/100k with prompt notices and no transition. Both teams signed version 8."
